hbo's preview for episode 3 has dropped  with a great sneak peek just how far in  time we're going and what we can expect  warning this is a full book and trailer  spoiler video so if you're wanting  something more non-spoilery check out my  weekly episode breakdowns which i'll  leave a link to in the description below  as well as for the hbo trailer now let's  get into it a pretty empty small council  with the dejected king viserys watching  his daughter rhaenyra saunter off if  there's one big theme this preview has  it's how rhaenyra deals with the  shocking news that her dad will wed her  best friend allison hightower it'll be  interesting if they actually show us  this wedding or if we simply fast  forward about one and a half to two  years from the events of episode two  this is my rough estimate considering  we'll see allison and viserys's first  child aegon ii named of course after the  first targaryen king aegon the conqueror  the same aegon who had the dream about a  great evil sweeping the land during a  long winter rhaenyra is wearing a really  interesting dress here is it one of her  normal ones or is it for some special  event the king himself also carries with  him the cat's paw dagger which he held  suspiciously close when he told renera  about aegon's dream otto tells his  daughter that aegon will be king this  would go against what viserys told  renera in episode 2 that she would  remain his heir i'm wondering if we're  at driftmark here the home of the  valerians this certainly doesn't look  like the red keep and there are these  sea snake type sculptures on the walls  and cups bonus points if you caught the  little doll here likely for aegon you'll  also notice alcent here with their hair  in this type of braid the same braid  will see her in while the king shows off  aegon to the crowd so i think we'll see  the king and queen going around the  realm to show the child off proving that  everything is well and good we aren't  exactly sure where this takes place  there's almost no descript banners  however take a look at two of the  prominent men watching aegon paraded  about one we've met the king's master of  laws lord lionel strong so i don't think  it's that far of a stretch to think that  the man beside him with a cane is one of  his sons sir loris strong he was after  all nicknamed lara's clubfoot because  his feet were twisted at birth the  historians who wrote the accounts found  in fire and blood find lloris to be one  of the most baffling characters whose  allegiances are never fully known this  makes him an especially dangerous  character i like this shot here of young  aegon being passed to his father where  you can make out he's been playing with  a little toy dragon from what i've read  aegon ii will be portrayed by three  different actors one as an infant a  child and an adult aegon will ride  sunfire who we haven't seen in the show  yet but whom we've seen in the previews  rhaenyra here looking a bit dejected in  what appears to be the small council  chamber you can make out some white hair  and possibly a dagger hilt so i'm  wondering if this is part of the first  shot we saw earlier whatever it is it  does not look like good news for  rhaenyra the king feeds his son in the  royal carriage while telling renera she  will soon be with her own son rhaenyra  will have her first child with coreless  valerian's son lenore roughly seven  years after the birth of aegon ii we've  seen the two together in the previews  however it looks like in this episode  the writers are setting up rhaenyra's  romance with sir kristen cole rhaenyra  will tell her father that she does not  wish to marry but she like him is bound  to duty i wonder if this scene is where  he tells her that she is to wed lenore  remember we did see otto and alison at  driftmark the home of the valerians so  it's possible all of this is connected  bonus points if you caught the little  cup for our cupbearer beside her in the  carriage alison tells what is likely  rhaenyra that things don't have to be  this way hinting that their friendship  is on the rocks this looks to take place  at the weirwood tree at the red keep  which is ironic since that's where we  saw their friendship at its strongest  rhaenyra tells her that no one is here  for her as we catch a glimpse of sir  kristen cole watching her ride off sir  kristen is tasked with rhaenyra's  protection so obviously he goes after  her we've seen a better shot of this in  the season trailer unfortunately for  rhaenyra she's stalked by a wild animal  a boar by the looks of it a boar is also  what mortally wounded robert baratheon  there also appears to be some armor here  on the bottom left sir kristen will  remove a sword from it but it's unclear  whether this person or armor was dead  slash here beforehand we've seen in the  trailer that kristen and rhaenyra spend  the night by campfire where rhaenyra  asked him do you think the realm will  ever accept me as that queen the  relationship between rhaenyra and sir  kristen is extremely interesting because  the book offers multiple scenarios on  how their love turns to poison in one  sir kristen rejects renera on account of  his kingsguard oath that he is never to  wed or have a partner and in the other  it's renera who will end up rejecting  sir kristen with septon ustus stating  that a targaryen was meant to be more  than a wife of a cell sword so i'm super  interested which direction the writers  will take this corliss warns that crab  feeder cragus rahar has dug his heels in  on bloodstone the largest of the islands  in the stepstones we also get our first  shot of corliss in this badass armor  this appears to be bloodstone under  siege giant balls of flame from siege  equipment on the island suggest the  ships here are corlisses to the left we  can make out a dragon this could either  be daemon's karaxis or lanor's sea smoke  the king here prepares to jab a bloody  spear i wonder if he'll be killing that  boar that attacked rhaenyra or perhaps  this is something else entirely corliss  and his men along with daemon use these  pieces to plan out their attack behind  daemon you can make out corliss's son  lenore who we last saw in episode 1 as a  child what ensues is a giant battle  between the valerian daemon alliance and  craga strahar backed by the triarchy  corliss exclaims that they're losing and  we even see damon shot with an arrow it  seems like one of those all is lost  moments until a dragon comes in to turn  the tides i actually think this is sea  smoke who is ridden by lenore this  doesn't look like caraxas to me and we  saw daemon injured by an arrow but it  also makes me question why damon didn't  just ride in with his dragon in the  first place perhaps he wants to prove  himself in battle without the help of  one that way no one can ever claim the  only reason he's as powerful as he is is  because of his dragon corliss did say to  him last episode that the stepstones  would be the perfect opportunity for him  to prove himself another question i have  is whether in this episode we'll see the  end of kragestrahar the war of the  stepstones was a two-year series of  battles in the book daemon ends up  beheading kragus with his sword dark  sister what i want to know is how long  these stepstones arc will go in the  series one of the trailers actually  shows prince damon returning to king's  landing holding what appears to be a  hammer could this be the same hammer  craga strahar used to nail his victims  corliss crowned damon the king of the  stepstones and narrow sea after his  victories there but the book has daemon  giving up that crown to viserys bending  the knee and the two reconcile with  damon getting a seat back on the small  council so that's it for the episode 3  preview i can't wait until next week  when i'm proven completely wrong be sure  to like and subscribe and if you haven't  seen my episode 2 breakdown be sure to  check that out you can also follow me on  twitter and instagram at think story yt  until next time remember it's a crispin  wasn't it  you
 

